{
  "transcript": "[Verse 1]\nSidewalk stage, the city sleeps\nConcrete beds and secrets keep\nEyes half-shut but wide with pain\nDraped in silence, soaked in rain\n\nHands like claws, frozen mid-air\nSwaying gently, unaware\nStatues made of skin and bone\nGallery of the overthrown\n\n[Chorus]\nLiving statues, stiff and numb\nHigh on apathy and heroin gum\nTime don\u2019t tick when you don\u2019t care\nWhen every breath\u2019s a cross to bear\n\nLiving statues, hollow eyes\nStill as death but not yet died\nFrozen souls in slow decay\nWelcome to downtown USA\n\n[Verse 2]\nTourists pass and snap their pics\nOf fentanyl parlor tricks\nBlink and miss the human cost\nThis city shines on what it\u2019s lost\n\nKnees are locked, spine like rust\nThey stand like tombstones in the dust\nNot alive and not quite dead\nTheir thoughts dissolved, their dreams misled\n\n[Chorus]\nLiving statues, frozen still\nOn corners shaped by greed and pills\nNodding off like urban ghosts\nOn taxpayer-funded overdose\n\nLiving statues, tragic art\nSilent screams and stopped-up hearts\nJust a pose on Market Street\nAnother soul the system beat\n\n[Bridge \u2013 Spoken / Screamed]\nNo rehab signs, just cop car lights\nNo housing plans, just sleepless nights\nYou call it \u201cblight,\u201d we call it \u201chell\u201d\nWhere the living rot but never fell\n\n[Final Chorus]\nLiving statues, keep your pose\nWhile the city shrugs and overdose grows\nStep around them, don't ask why\nJust blame the weak and walk on by\n\nLiving statues, stand in shame\nNot theirs \u2014 but ours, in freedom\u2019s name\nSo freeze the frame, this ain\u2019t a dream\nIt\u2019s America, dressed in dopamine\n",
